 ## Overview
-2D Transfer Function Volume Rendering extends the 1D Lookup Table with Interpolation method by modulating opacity based on the gradient magnitude of the volume data, in addition to the scalar voxel value [S2, S3, unofficial]. This approach solves the ambiguity of 1D transfer functions where different materials may share similar intensity values but differ in surface smoothness or texture [S3, unofficial]. By incorporating gradient information, it provides superior tissue differentiation and emphasizes material boundaries and internal structures [S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from the parent [Hardcoded Transfer Function](1098-hardcoded-transfer-function.md) by using a 2D lookup texture (Intensity vs. Gradient) rather than a 1D array, and from the sibling [Tent Alpha Transfer Function](3031-tent-alpha-transfer-function.md) by utilizing gradient magnitude for modulation rather than a specific tent-shaped alpha curve.
+2D Transfer Function Volume Rendering extends a 1D scalar-to-color/opacity transfer function by modulating opacity with gradient magnitude, emphasizing material boundaries and internal structures [S2, unofficial]. This approach solves the ambiguity of 1D transfer functions where different materials share similar intensity values but differ in surface smoothness or texture [S3, unofficial]. By incorporating gradient information, it provides superior tissue differentiation and more intuitive volume design [S3, unofficial]. It differs from the parent [Hardcoded Transfer Function](1098-hardcoded-transfer-function.md) by using a 2D lookup texture (Intensity vs. Gradient) rather than a 1D array, and from the sibling [Tent Alpha Transfer Function](3031-tent-alpha-transfer-function.md) by utilizing gradient magnitude for modulation rather than a specific tent-shaped alpha curve [S2, unofficial].
 
